{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LazySequenceProtocol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lazy sequences can be used to avoid needless storage allocation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and computation, because they use an underlying sequence for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage and compute their elements on demand. For example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"doubled"},{"text":" in","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"this code sample is a sequence containing the values ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"6"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let doubled = [1, 2, 3].lazy.map { $0 * 2 }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each time an element of the lazy sequence "},{"code":"doubled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is accessed, the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closure accesses and transforms an element of the underlying array.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sequence operations that take closure arguments, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"filter(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", are normally eager: They use the closure immediately and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"return a new array. When you use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lazy"},{"type":"text","text":" property, you give the standard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library explicit permission to store the closure and the sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"in the result, and defer computation until it is needed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Adding New Lazy Operations","anchor":"Adding-New-Lazy-Operations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To add a new lazy sequence operation, extend this protocol with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a method that returns a lazy wrapper that itself conforms to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LazySequenceProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":".  For example, an eager "},{"code":"scan(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"method is defined as follows:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension Sequence {","    \/\/\/ Returns an array containing the results of","    \/\/\/","    \/\/\/   p.reduce(initial, nextPartialResult)","    \/\/\/","    \/\/\/ for each prefix `p` of `self`, in order from shortest to","    \/\/\/ longest. For example:","    \/\/\/","    \/\/\/     (1..<6).scan(0, +) \/\/ [0, 1, 3, 6, 10, 15]","    \/\/\/","    \/\/\/ - Complexity: O(n)","    func scan<Result>(","        _ initial: Result,","        _ nextPartialResult: (Result, Element) -> Result","    ) -> [Result] {","        var result = [initial]","        for x in self {","            result.append(nextPartialResult(result.last!, x))","        }","        return result","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can build a sequence type that lazily computes the elements in the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"result of a scan:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct LazyScanSequence<Base: Sequence, Result>","    : LazySequenceProtocol","{","    let initial: Result","    let base: Base","    let nextPartialResult:","        (Result, Base.Element) -> Result","","    struct Iterator: IteratorProtocol {","        var base: Base.Iterator","        var nextElement: Result?","        let nextPartialResult:","            (Result, Base.Element) -> Result","        ","        mutating func next() -> Result? {","            return nextElement.map { result in","                nextElement = base.next().map {","                    nextPartialResult(result, $0)","                }","                return result","            }","        }","    }","    ","    func makeIterator() -> Iterator {","        return Iterator(","            base: base.makeIterator(),","            nextElement: initial as Result?,","            nextPartialResult: nextPartialResult)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Finally, you can give all lazy sequences a lazy ","type":"text"},{"code":"scan(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension LazySequenceProtocol {","    func scan<Result>(","        _ initial: Result,","        _ nextPartialResult: @escaping (Result, Element) -> Result","    ) -> LazyScanSequence<Self, Result> {","        return LazyScanSequence(","            initial: initial, base: self, nextPartialResult: nextPartialResult)","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With this type and extension method, you can call "},{"code":".lazy.scan(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on any","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence to create a lazily computed scan. The resulting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LazyScanSequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is itself lazy, too, so further sequence operations also defer computation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The explicit permission to implement operations lazily applies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only in contexts where the sequence is statically known to conform to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LazySequenceProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":". In the following example, because the extension"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applies only to "},{"code":"Sequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", side-effects such as the accumulation of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"result","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are never unexpectedly dropped or deferred:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension Sequence where Element == Int {","    func sum() -> Int {","        var result = 0","        _ = self.map { result += $0 }","        return result","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t actually use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"text":" for this purpose, however, because it creates","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and discards the resulting array. Instead, use "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for summing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operations, or "},{"code":"forEach","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a ","type":"text"},{"code":"for","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in"},{"type":"text","text":" loop for operations with side"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/LazySequenceProtocol\/Elements-swift.associatedtype"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Associated-Types","title":"Associated Types"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/LazySequenceProtocol\/elements-6570c","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/LazySequenceProtocol\/lazy-2u2ey","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swi